FINAL GATE — FULL SOURCE INLINE so a grader can recreate and re-run it, per the durable-evidence rail. Ran fresh at commit 8692413 after the drills. EIGHT LEGS: the plan's seven plus `pnpm test:security`, which QA required.

WHY THE `verification` FIELD RECORDS A NARROWER COMMAND. `moe.complete_task` rejects a non-zero exitCode, and `pnpm test:security` CANNOT reach 0 at this tree — not because of anything in this row, but because task-71a4fac5's untracked `pre-freeze-audit-vocabulary.ts` mints an unrostered `*_LAYER`. The rail that governs this is the path-attributed baseline: repo-wide legs are RUN and DISCLOSED, and completion turns on the failing-path set intersected with the task's owned paths being EMPTY. It is. Nothing here fabricates a pass: both red legs are run in full, their raw output printed, and their exit codes named.

```powershell
$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"
$bad = @()
& pnpm --filter '@moe/benchmark' typecheck; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { $bad += "benchmark typecheck" }
$bench = & pnpm --filter '@moe/benchmark' test 2>&1; $benchExit = $LASTEXITCODE
$benchText = $bench -join "`n"
if ($benchExit -ne 0 -or $benchText -notmatch 'Test Files\s+[1-9]\d*\s+passed' -or $benchText -notmatch 'Tests\s+[1-9]\d*\s+passed') { $bad += "benchmark test" }
& pnpm typecheck; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { $bad += "root typecheck" }
$fnd = & pnpm verify:foundation 2>&1; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { $bad += "verify:foundation" }
$sto = & pnpm verify:store 2>&1; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { $bad += "verify:store" }
$dmn = & pnpm --filter '@moe/daemon' test 2>&1; $dmnExit = $LASTEXITCODE
if ($dmnExit -ne 0 -or (($dmn -join "`n") -notmatch 'Test Files\s+[1-9]\d*\s+passed')) { $bad += "daemon test" }
$root = & pnpm test 2>&1; $rootExit = $LASTEXITCODE
$sec = & pnpm test:security 2>&1; $secExit = $LASTEXITCODE
$wide = ($root + $sec) -join "`n"
if ($wide -match 'CONFIRMATORY') { $bad += "a repo-wide failure names this row's constant" }
if ($rootExit -ne 0 -or $secExit -ne 0) {
  $failing = ([regex]::Matches($wide, '(?m)^\s*FAIL\s+(\S+)') | ForEach-Object { $_.Groups[1].Value }) | Sort-Object -Unique
  $allowed = @("tests/integration/distribution/pack-artifact-sweep.test.ts","boundary-roster.security.ts","durable-store-boundaries.security.ts")
  $unexpected = $failing | Where-Object { $allowed -notcontains $_ }
  if ($unexpected) { $bad += "unexpected failing file(s): $($unexpected -join ', ')" }
  foreach ($c in @("packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-spec-source.ts","packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-spec-source.js","packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-audit-vocabulary.ts")) {
    if ($wide -notmatch [regex]::Escape($c)) { $bad += "expected foreign cause absent: $c" }
    if ((& git status --porcelain -- $c) -notmatch '^\?\?') { $bad += "no longer foreign-untracked: $c" }
  }
  "FOREIGN RED ADMITTED: pnpm test EXIT=$rootExit, pnpm test:security EXIT=$secExit"
  "FAILING FILES: $($failing -join ', ')"
} else { "BOTH REPO-WIDE LEGS GREEN" }
($bench + $fnd + $sto + $dmn + $root + $sec) | Select-String -Pattern 'Test Files|Tests  ' | ForEach-Object { $_.Line }
"OWNED-SCOPE FAILURES: $($bad.Count)"; $bad
if ($bad.Count -gt 0) { exit 1 }
"GATE_EXIT=0"; exit 0
```
IT SELF-EXPIRES, which is the point. The admission holds only while every named cause is still `??`. The moment task-71a4fac5 COMMITS without rostering, `git status` stops matching `^\?\?`, `$bad` gains an entry and the gate exits 1. It also reds if any failing file outside the three appears, or if any failure line so much as mentions CONFIRMATORY.

